== 3. Proposition 5.2(c) direct form and 5.2(d) ==
  Pr[beta(M^(T)) = q/2] >= (1 - e^(-1/delta)) delta > 0.63 delta on the grid; least ratio Pr/(0.63 delta) = 1.0037
  0.63/(2 ln 2) = 0.45445 > 0.45; 1 - e^(-1) = 0.63212 > 0.63
  engine, n=6, delta=0.5: Pr[beta(M^(T)) = q/2 = 0.1667] = 0.456104; formula 0.456104
  delta1=0.05, delta2=0.05: direct factor 1/(d1+d2) = 10.000  <  (1 + ln(1/d1)/ln(W/w))/d2 = 79.915 (ln(W/w)=1)
  delta1=0.01, delta2=0.09: direct factor 1/(d1+d2) = 10.000  <  (1 + ln(1/d1)/ln(W/w))/d2 = 62.280 (ln(W/w)=1)
  delta1=0.5, delta2=0.4: direct factor 1/(d1+d2) = 1.111  <  (1 + ln(1/d1)/ln(W/w))/d2 = 4.233 (ln(W/w)=1)

