== 8. 'Compute' (Section 2): rejection sampling from the posterior ==
  posterior: 0:0.0376, 10:0.7249, 110:0.2375, 111:0.0000
  accepted : 0:0.0389, 10:0.7244, 110:0.2368, 111:0.0000  (100000 draws)
  mean trials per draw = 93.316; 1/xi(D) = 92.786; 2^K / P(D) = 390.625 (bound holds: True)
  with an incomplete code, e.g. {0, 10} (Kraft sum 3/4), the reading never ends after the prefix 11:
    probability 1/4 per trial; a reader cannot in general decide that a prefix has no extension in a decidable code,
    so the expected time per draw is infinite unless the code is complete or dead prefixes are decidable.
    stochastic human (Bern 0.8), n=10 answers: 1/xi(D) = 9.234e+02 (grows like exp(n x entropy))
    stochastic human (Bern 0.8), n=50 answers: 1/xi(D) = 5.309e+14 (grows like exp(n x entropy))
    stochastic human (Bern 0.8), n=100 answers: 1/xi(D) = 2.699e+21 (grows like exp(n x entropy))
